WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:03.400
A microphone on stage picks up the speaker.

2
00:00:03.490 --> 00:00:07.200
The sound loops back, builds, and becomes a howl.

3
00:00:07.750 --> 00:00:10.050
Today, engineers pull the fader down,

4
00:00:10.200 --> 00:00:13.900
or notch out frequencies — and that costs volume and tone.

5
00:00:14.900 --> 00:00:18.250
Nullyn AI sits inline between the mic and the console.

6
00:00:18.400 --> 00:00:21.450
It listens to both the microphone and the speaker feed,

7
00:00:21.630 --> 00:00:26.200
predicts the feedback path in real time,
and removes the loop before it rings.

8
00:00:26.540 --> 00:00:29.600
The voice and the instruments stay natural.

9
00:00:30.120 --> 00:00:34.250
Version one runs on a laptop
with a USB audio interface.

10
00:00:34.430 --> 00:00:37.200
Version two is our own dedicated box.

11
00:00:37.410 --> 00:00:40.000
Version three deploys at scale.

12
00:00:40.450 --> 00:00:45.400
Nullyn AI. More gain before feedback,
without wrecking the sound.

13
00:00:46.000 --> 00:00:49.200
nullyn.ai
